# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

Three error views in `apps/web` get a **Try again** button that re-runs only the step that failed:
- the card sheet's statistics block reloads the stats;
- the creator's script-check alert runs the check again on the same source, so Save comes back without an edit;
- a failed GIF share keeps the GIF it already made, and Try again hands that same file to the share sheet again without re-encoding.

Each surface gets one test that goes failure → retry → success. The existing tests still pass, which shows the normal paths are unchanged.

## Files to touch

| Path | new/change | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/stats/CardStatsBlock.tsx` | change | `attempt` state in the load effect's deps; a Try again button in the error view, shown only on a load error |
| `apps/web/src/cards/inspect/inspect.css` | change | new rule `.inspect-stats-retry` |
| `apps/web/src/stats/CardStatsBlock.test.tsx` | change | import `fireEvent`; const `SPARK_PUP`; new `describe` with 2 tests |
| `apps/web/src/creator/Creator.tsx` | change | `useScriptCheck` returns `[ScriptCheck, () => void]`; `Editor`'s script-check alert gets Try again |
| `apps/web/src/creator/testids.ts` | change | `checkRetry: "creator-check-retry"` |
| `apps/web/src/creator/Creator.test.tsx` | change | new `describe` with 1 test |
| `apps/web/src/replay/ShareGif.tsx` | change | `type GifReady`; the `failed` variant of `GifPhase` gets `ready: GifReady \| null`; `make`'s catch; `send`; `gifTestid.retry`; retry button in `ShareGif` |
| `apps/web/src/replay/ShareGif.test.tsx` | change | 2 assertions added to "an export that fails says why"; 1 new test |

Do not touch: `apps/web/src/wasm/index.ts` (`luauBindings` already sets `luau = null` after a failed load, so a second check imports the module again), `apps/web/src/i18n/zh-CN.json` (it already has `"Try again"`, and `i18n.test.ts` requires a zh-CN entry for every `t()` literal, so add no new sentence), `e2e/` (its testids file copies only the ids the e2e specs use), every crate, `spec/`, `crates/cards/patches/` (a client-only change needs no patch fragment, like #1811). No spec section or ruling governs this: §9.11, §12.9 and R513000 say nothing about retrying, so the change adds no ruling.

## Steps

1. **`apps/web/src/stats/CardStatsBlock.tsx`, `CardStatsBlock`.**
   - Right after `const [error, setError] = useState(false);` add:
     ```tsx
     /** Bumped by Try again, which loads the card's statistics again. */
     const [attempt, setAttempt] = useState(0);
     ```
   - Change the load effect's deps from `[cardId]` to `[cardId, attempt]`. Leave the effect body alone: it already resets `loading` and `error`.
   - In the `if (error || !stat)` view, right after the `<p className="inspect-stats-unavailable">…</p>` line, add:
     ```tsx
     {error ? (
       <button type="button" className="inspect-stats-retry" onClick={() => setAttempt((before) => before + 1)}>
         {t("Try again")}
       </button>
     ) : null}
     ```
   - Add no testid. A new `INSPECT_*` id would have to be copied into e2e's A14 block, so the test finds the button by its role instead.

2. **`apps/web/src/cards/inspect/inspect.css`.** Right after the `.inspect-stats-loading, .inspect-stats-unavailable { … }` rule, add:
   ```css
   .inspect-stats-retry {
     align-self: flex-start;
   }
   ```
   `.inspect-stats` is a flex column, so without this rule the button would stretch across the whole block.

3. **`apps/web/src/creator/Creator.tsx`, `useScriptCheck`.**
   - Change the signature to `function useScriptCheck(card: CustomCard, check: CreatorApi["check"]): [ScriptCheck, () => void]`.
   - After the `result` state, add:
     ```tsx
     /** Bumped by the failed check's Try again, which asks again for the same script. */
     const [attempt, setAttempt] = useState(0);
     ```
   - Change the effect deps to `[source, check, attempt]`.
   - Replace `return result;` with:
     ```tsx
     const retry = useCallback(() => setAttempt((before) => before + 1), []);
     return [result, retry];
     ```
     `useCallback` is already imported.
   - Add one sentence to the hook's doc comment: "The second value asks again after a check that failed, with no edit."

4. **`apps/web/src/creator/Creator.tsx`, `Editor`.**
   - Change `const script = useScriptCheck(card, check);` to `const [script, retryCheck] = useScriptCheck(card, check);`.
   - Replace the `script.kind === "failed"` block's `<p className="creator-error" role="alert">…</p>` with the following. It copies the stale-save block's layout:
     ```tsx
     <div className="creator-error" role="alert">
       <p>{t("The script could not be checked: {message}", { message: script.message })}</p>
       <button type="button" className="button-secondary" data-testid={creatorTestid.checkRetry} onClick={retryCheck}>
         {t("Try again")}
       </button>
     </div>
     ```

5. **`apps/web/src/creator/testids.ts`.** Right after `checking: "creator-checking",` add `checkRetry: "creator-check-retry",`.

6. **`apps/web/src/replay/ShareGif.tsx`.**
   - In `gifTestid`, after `share: "replay-gif-share",` add `retry: "replay-gif-retry",`.
   - Replace the `GifPhase` type with:
     ```ts
     /** A made GIF, and whether the device can hand it to the share sheet (else Share downloads it). */
     type GifReady = { kind: "ready"; file: File; share: boolean };

     export type GifPhase =
       | { kind: "idle" }
       | { kind: "working"; frame: number; frames: number; attempt: number; attempts: number }
       | GifReady
       | { kind: "tooBig" }
       // `ready`: the made GIF whose share failed, which Try again shares again without drawing it anew;
       // null when the export itself failed, where Make GIF is the way on.
       | { kind: "failed"; message: string; ready: GifReady | null };
     ```
   - In `make`'s `catch`, add `ready: null` to the `setPhase({ kind: "failed", … })` object.
   - Replace the body of `send` with:
     ```ts
     // Share, or Try again after a share that failed: the made GIF either way, never drawn again.
     const ready = phase.kind === "ready" ? phase : phase.kind === "failed" ? phase.ready : null;
     if (ready === null || loaded.current === null) return;
     setPhase(ready);
     loaded.current.shareGif(ready.file).catch((cause: unknown) => {
       // A dismissed share sheet is the viewer's answer, not a failure.
       if (!isAbort(cause)) setPhase({ kind: "failed", message: cause instanceof Error ? cause.message : String(cause), ready });
     });
     ```
     `shareGif` must still be called synchronously inside the click. It is, because `loaded.current` is already set.
   - In `ShareGif`, right after the `phase.kind === "failed"` alert block, add:
     ```tsx
     {phase.kind === "failed" && phase.ready !== null ? (
       <button type="button" data-testid={gifTestid.retry} onClick={gif.send}>
         {t("Try again")}
       </button>
     ) : null}
     ```

7. Add the tests below.

## Tests

**`apps/web/src/stats/CardStatsBlock.test.tsx`**
- Add `fireEvent` to the `@testing-library/react` import.
- After `afterEach`, add `const SPARK_PUP = {…}`, a copy of the `core-001` card object from the first test.
- Add a new `describe("CardStatsBlock after a load that failed", …)`, with no R-id in any title:
  - `it("offers Try again, which loads the card's statistics again")`:
    - Set up `const fetchMock = vi.fn().mockRejectedValueOnce(new TypeError("Failed to fetch")).mockResolvedValueOnce(new Response(JSON.stringify(mockStatsResponse(SPARK_PUP)), { status: 200 }))`, then `vi.stubGlobal("fetch", fetchMock)` and render `cardId="core-001"`.
    - `await screen.findByText("Statistics unavailable", undefined, SLOW)`.
    - `fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Try again" }))`.
    - `await screen.findByText("Played Δ", undefined, SLOW)`; `"+20%"` is shown; `"Statistics unavailable"` is gone; `fetchMock` was called 2 times.
  - `it("offers no Try again

